TITLE:: MS20SK
summary:: Linear Korg-35 Sallen-Key low-pass and authentic MS-20 high-pass filter
categories:: UGens>Filters>Linear
related:: Guides/Filtra, Classes/MS20TPT, Classes/MS20Diode, Classes/MS20OTA

DESCRIPTION::
MS20SK provides a linear, component-topology-informed digital model of the early Korg-35 Sallen-Key filter from the Korg MS-10 and MS-20 synthesizers. It is discretized via the prewarped Bilinear Transform (Tustin) implemented as a Transposed Direct Form II biquad.

Unlike cookbook 2nd-order filters:
LIST::
## The strong inter-stage loading of the two RC sections is preserved in the denominator damping term:
code::
D(s) = (s / \omega_0)^2 + (3 - K) (s / \omega_0) + 1
::
where strong loading contributes an extra damping term (+1), requiring teletype::K = 3:: (rather than teletype::K = 2:: as in buffered stages) for infinite-Q / self-oscillation.
## The High-Pass mode (mode 1) models the historically authentic MS-20 circuit topology where the LP input is grounded and the signal is injected at the bottom of capacitor C2. This produces a numerator of:
code::
N_HP(s) = (s / \omega_0)^2 + 2 (s / \omega_0)
::
resulting in a 6 dB/octave asymptotic low-frequency attenuation rather than a standard 12 dB/octave high-pass slope, while retaining the full 2nd-order resonant denominator.
::

NOTE::
MS20SK is a linear reference model without active diode or amplifier saturation. For linear stability, resonance teletype::res:: in [0, 1] is mapped to feedback gain teletype::K = res * 2.95:: (clamped to teletype::[0, 2.95]::, corresponding to maximum Q = 20). Self-oscillation (K = 3) is intentionally bounded below 3.0 to prevent unbounded numerical divergence.
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar
Create an audio-rate MS20SK filter instance.

ARGUMENT:: in
Audio rate input signal.

ARGUMENT:: freq
Cutoff / natural frequency in Hz (internally clamped to [10 Hz, 0.49 * sampleRate]). Supports scalar, control-rate (kr), and audio-rate (ar) modulation for sample-accurate filter FM.

ARGUMENT:: res
Normalized resonance control in [0.0, 1.0]. Maps linearly to feedback parameter teletype::K = res * 2.95::, with damping teletype::(3 - K):: and pole teletype::Q = 1 / (3 - K)::.

ARGUMENT:: mode
Filter mode selection (evaluated at synth instantiation / i-rate):
LIST::
## 0 = Low-pass filter (12 dB/octave roll-off, unity DC gain)
## 1 = Authentic MS-20 High-pass filter (6 dB/octave low-frequency roll-off, 2nd-order resonance peak, unity high-frequency gain)
::

returns:: An audio-rate UGen output.

EXAMPLES::

Three practical examples demonstrating LP sweep, HP sweep, and audible resonance sweep:

code::
s.boot;

// 1. Noise Low-Pass sweep (12 dB/octave roll-off)
(
x = {
    var src = WhiteNoise.ar(0.15);
    var cutoff = SinOsc.kr(0.2).exprange(100, 8000);
    var sig = MS20SK.ar(src, freq: cutoff, res: 0.3, mode: 0);
    sig ! 2
}.play;
)
x.free;

// 2. Noise High-Pass sweep (authentic 6 dB/octave low-frequency slope)
(
x = {
    var src = WhiteNoise.ar(0.15);
    var cutoff = SinOsc.kr(0.2).exprange(80, 6000);
    var sig = MS20SK.ar(src, freq: cutoff, res: 0.4, mode: 1);
    sig ! 2
}.play;
)
x.free;

// 3. Audible resonance sweep (Sawtooth waveform with high resonance)
(
x = {
    var src = Saw.ar([55, 55.4]) * 0.12;
    var cutoff = XLine.kr(120, 6000, 8);
    // res = 0.85 yields K ≈ 2.5, Q ≈ 2.0 with a strong resonant peak
    var sig = MS20SK.ar(src, freq: cutoff, res: 0.85, mode: 0);
    sig
}.play;
)
x.free;
::
